@startuml
title Option A — push timeout, SMS failover and late receipts
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
participant "Orchestrator /\ndurable timer scanner" as FSM
database "PostgreSQL\nledger + outbox" as DB
participant "Relay + Kafka" as Q
participant "Channel worker" as Worker
participant "SMS-A / SMS-B" as SMS
participant "Email provider" as Email
participant "Receipt Gateway" as Receipt

note over FSM, DB: PUSH attempt accepted at t0; no app receipt.\nDurable push deadline = t0+8s.
FSM -> DB: At deadline: lock notification; check receipt/state/version
alt Receipt already committed
  DB --> FSM: DELIVERED; timer becomes no-op
else No delivery evidence
  FSM -> DB: CAS next attempt SMS-A\nrecord attempt + command outbox atomically
  Q -> Worker: SMS-A attempt_id (may be redelivered)
  Worker -> DB: Claim; final pre-send check; durable DISPATCHING
  Worker -> SMS: Send(same attempt_id idempotency key)
  alt Explicit permanent / provider rejection
    SMS --> Worker: Definitively not accepted
    Worker -> DB: Record failure + outbox
    FSM -> DB: CAS create SMS-B attempt (independent quota)
    Q -> Worker: SMS-B attempt
    Worker -> SMS: Send via SMS-B with its own attempt_id
  else Network timeout / result unknown
    Worker -> DB: UNKNOWN + durable reconcile deadline
    Worker -> SMS: Query status by attempt_id
    note over Worker, SMS: No blind retry with a new key.\nSame-provider resend only with contractual idempotency.
    alt No conclusive receipt by t0+30s
      FSM -> DB: CAS create eligible EMAIL attempt\nrecord residual-duplicate risk
      Q -> Worker: Email attempt
      Worker -> Email: Send same notification_id
    end
  else Provider acceptance
    SMS --> Worker: message_id (not delivery proof)
    Worker -> DB: WAIT_RECEIPT
  end
end
SMS -> Receipt: Signed delivered receipt (possibly late / repeated)
Receipt -> DB: Dedup receipt; monotonic CAS DELIVERED\ncancel only attempts not yet dispatched
note over DB, Worker: Receipt racing with a timer is serialized by CAS.\nAn already-sent SMS cannot be recalled.\nLate cross-channel duplicates remain possible and are measured.
FSM -> DB: At t0+60s without proof: record SLO breach; continue recovery
FSM -> DB: At 24h unresolved: ESCALATED + incident; no silent drop
@enduml
